   39062/   1E56A :                     ; ============================
   39063/   1E56A :                     
   39064/   1E56A : (MACRO)             	even
   39065/   1E56A :                     
   39066/   1E56A :                     ; ------------------------------------------------------
   39067/   1E56A :                     ; Stat increase pointers and EXP values
   39068/   1E56A :                     ;
   39069/   1E56A :                     ; Stat increase
   39070/   1E56A :                     ;
   39071/   1E56A :                     ; 1 = HP
   39072/   1E56A :                     ; 2 = TP
   39073/   1E56A :                     ; 3 = Damage
   39074/   1E56A :                     ; 4 = Defense
   39075/   1E56A :                     ; 5 = Speed
   39076/   1E56A :                     ; 6 = Luck
   39077/   1E56A :                     ; 7 = Skill
   39078/   1E56A :                     ;
   39079/   1E56A :                     ; You can easily extend EXP tables and make characters reach lv 99 if you wish.
   39080/   1E56A :                     ; Keep in mind that the values for EXP are the total EXP the a character needs to learn
   39081/   1E56A :                     ; and not the EXP needed to go up a level. So for a certain level, make sure you don't have values equal or less than
   39082/   1E56A :                     ; the previous levels or there will most likely be bugs.
   39083/   1E56A :                     ;
   39084/   1E56A :                     ; Speaking of bugs, the last value of the table for EXP (the one before the 0's) will not
   39085/   1E56A :                     ; count as a level up, meaning it there won't be stat increases and the game
   39086/   1E56A :                     ; will not update the level counter. Remove the -1 from the count before the
   39087/   1E56A :                     ; start of that table. So for example:
   39088/   1E56A :                     ;
   39089/   1E56A :                     ; dc.l	(RhysExpPoints_End-RhysExpPoints)/4-1
   39090/   1E56A :                     ;
   39091/   1E56A :                     ; becomes
   39092/   1E56A :                     ;
   39093/   1E56A :                     ; dc.l	(RhysExpPoints_End-RhysExpPoints)/4
   39094/   1E56A :                     ; ------------------------------------------------------
   39095/   1E56A :                     
